ideas.hypothesis:
Verification pays off only for an error form that some cheap scorer ranks below gold:
- Supa likelihood;
- Titan-OFF likelihood;
- T2-ON or 3-adapter likelihood;
- a retrospective hidden-state probe.
Predictions:
- ledger digit slips: ranked correctly by ensemble likelihood at ≥ 0.85;
- ledger void applied-anyway: ranked correctly by OFF likelihood even though OFF generates them (a generator–verifier gap, as in BWM F-02);
- register wrong-branch, unreduced-sum, and P copy / state+add foils: no scorer reaches 0.7, so those cells need decomposition (ideas 2 and 3), not verification.
This turns 'when does verification pay off?' into a measured table per cell, before more GPU time goes into rollouts.

