ideas.hypothesis:
(a) BWM's F-03 confidence-gated deferral to the adapter-off base replicates on fresh sealed RW2 keys at never-used limits, with the band frozen at (0.01, 0.5) and no reselection:
- flip-double accuracy F_LM <= 0.5 -> gated >= 0.85;
- in-distribution within -1 pp;
- BFS-256 range planning improves.
(b) A learned gate restricted to model-internal signals (F's legality margin, the verifier's margin, Mahalanobis novelty of mid-layer answer-slot states vs training keys) repairs a significant share of the confident below-range errors (F-06), where no confidence-only gate works. A control gate with shuffled labels does not, and an input-feature gate is shown to be just the code rule. This uses RCWM's probe-selectivity discipline to keep the gate from smuggling in the rule.
